## Conventions fixed here, for the dataset workers (12 October 2026)

- uv is the pixel centre, v downwards, so `bank.uv_grid` and `gl_FragCoord` give identical sample points; non-square canvases are handled by an explicit `aspect` param when a block needs isotropy. (12 October 2026)
- Blocks take every parameter as a function argument (no uniforms in block.glsl), so one block can serve several layers; helpers carry the `<id>_` prefix. (12 October 2026)
- Mask blocks return `(1, 1, 1, m)`; a layer's alpha is `s.a * mask.a * luma(mask.rgb)`, so a colour block can also act as a mask by its luminance. (12 October 2026)
- Twins load with `sys.dont_write_bytecode` so no `__pycache__` lands in the dataset; `ZRMD_SHADER_BANK` points the bank at another folder. (12 October 2026)

